AKAZAWA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONISHI, TOMOYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIROSE NAOKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IZAWA KUNISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAZAWA MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ONISHI TOMOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIROSE, NAOKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IZAWA, KUNISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZAWA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONISHI, TOMOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process which comprises converting a  alpha -amino acid ester into the corresponding imine to thereby protect the amino group of the ester, reacting the imine with a halomethyllithium to form an N-protected  alpha -amino halomethyl ketone, and treating this N-protected  alpha -amino halomethyl ketone with an acid to obtain a  alpha -amino halomethyl ketone. This process is suitable for industrial production and permits economical and efficient production of  alpha -amino halomethyl ketones and compounds related thereto.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé qui consiste à convertir un ester d'alpha-aminoacide en imine correspondante, de manière à protéger le groupe amino de l'ester. On fait réagir l'imine avec un halométhyllithium pour former une alpha-amino halométhyl-cétone à protection N, qui est ensuite traitée avec un acide de manière à donner une alpha-amino halométhyl-cétone. Ce procédé est approprié à la fabrication industrielle et permet d'assurer une production économique et efficace d'alpha-amino halométhyl-cétones et de composés connexes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>